{"topic": "Gradient Descent and Learning Rate", "audience": "", "referenceMaterial": "[none provided]", "allowedTypes": {"chart": "Author a chart block for a LectureDoc lecture — a data chart (bar/line/area/scatter) rendered via Observable Plot, theme-aware. Reach for it whenever a page shows numeric comparison, trend over time, share/composition, or correlation — anything where seeing the shape of the numbers beats reading them. Prefer a chart over a table when magnitude/trend/relationship is the point; use a table only for exact nominal lookup where values are not being compared. Produces schema-valid chart block JSON.", "runnable": "Author a runnable (edit → Run) code cell block for a LectureDoc lecture — an in-browser Python (Pyodide) + JavaScript editor with a console and a result chart. Reach for it whenever the student should learn by writing/modifying and actually executing code themselves: implementing an algorithm by hand, tuning parameters and seeing the effect, exploratory what-if coding. Use a plain `code` block instead for read-only display the student will not run. Produces schema-valid runnable block JSON.", "hero": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "statement": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "pullquote": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "list": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "agenda": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "callout": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "formula": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "flow": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "table": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "code": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "compare": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "grid": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "timeline": "Author static content blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, flow, table, code, compare, grid. Use when a lecture needs prose/narrative/layout (not an interactive sim, quiz, or code runtime). Produces schema-valid block JSON.", "freeform": "Author a freeform block for a LectureDoc lecture — the long-tail fallback for a visual relationship that none of the formal block types can express, drawn as inline SVG/HTML restricted to theme colour tokens. Reach for it only after checking the structured types: graph covers trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts; chart covers data; diagram covers fixed shapes; grid and sim.widget cover custom layouts and interactive pieces. When it genuinely is the right tool it now renders as normal page content, so use it without hedging. Produces schema-valid freeform block JSON.", "stats": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "diagram": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "graph": "Author stats (KPI number cards), diagram (fixed structural shapes — cycle/pyramid/staircase/snake/arrow-seq/circular-grid/connected-circles) and graph (true node-edge trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts, rendered as real layered SVG) blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Reach for stats to spotlight a handful of standalone key numbers; reach for graph whenever nodes have *named relationships* — parent/child, dependency, branch, merge — since it is the only block type with an edges field; reach for diagram only for a fixed decorative shape with no explicit edges. Use flow for a simple linear 2-3 step sequence. Produces schema-valid stats/diagram/graph block JSON.", "quiz": "Author a quiz block for a LectureDoc lecture — objective (multiple-choice, auto-graded) or subjective (open discussion prompt). Reach for it whenever a page should check understanding or provoke reflection rather than only present — at least one per lecture is encouraged. Objective for a checkable fact/skill, subjective for open-ended thinking. Produces schema-valid quiz block JSON.", "sim": "Author a sim (simulation) block for a LectureDoc lecture — a parameter-driven interactive that recomputes and redraws in-browser as the student changes inputs. Reach for it whenever a quantitative or mechanistic process becomes clearer by letting the student turn a knob and watch the outcome change (physics/chem dynamics, algorithm behaviour, parameter sensitivity); pick a sim over a static chart when the interaction itself is the teaching point. Engines are chosen at build time: dynamics1d/searchCompare (declarative restricted-expression math → line charts), custom (sandboxed compute), widget (live canvas/SVG animation, geometric construction, or arbitrary mouse interaction). Skip it when the topic has no quantifiable/mechanistic process to manipulate — a sim with no real parameter to turn is decoration, not interaction. Produces schema-valid sim block JSON."}, "currentBrief": {"objective": "学生能复述本页核心结论", "keyClaim": "随机梯度下降：噪声反而能帮忙", "misconception": "", "visualTask": "视觉直接编码本页核心关系", "evidencePolicy": "none"}, "currentScene": {"id": "sgd-noise", "kind": "content", "eyebrow": "进阶技巧", "headline": "随机梯度下降：噪声反而能帮忙", "lead": "SGD 的梯度噪声有助于逃离局部极小，且计算效率更高。", "notes": "解释为什么实际中 SGD 比全批量更常用。", "blocks": [{"type": "list", "items": [{"lead": "逃离局部极小", "text": "每次只用一个样本的梯度，**噪声**让参数有机会跳出浅谷，找到更优解。", "icon": "user"}, {"lead": "计算效率高", "text": "每步仅需 $O(1)$ 样本，适合大规模数据集，迭代速度远快于全批量。", "icon": "zap"}, {"lead": "隐式正则化", "text": "随机采样引入的方差相当于一种**隐式正则项**，有助于泛化。", "icon": "camera"}], "id": "sgd-noise-r1"}, {"type": "sim", "engine": "widget", "html": "<style>
  .sgd-widget {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 12px);
    padding: 16px 20px 20px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    height: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .sgd-widget canvas {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--card);
    border-radius: var(--radius, 8px);
    cursor: default;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
  }
  .controls-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .controls-row label {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text2);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .controls-row input[type=range] {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 80px;
    accent-color: var(--accent);
    height: 4px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .val {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent);
    min-width: 36px;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .step-readout {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text2);
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 2px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--radius, 6px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .btn-group {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  .btn-group button {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 12px;
    padding: 4px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius, 6px);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 150ms, border-color 150ms, transform 120ms;
    letter-spacing: .03em;
  }
  .btn-group button:hover {
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .btn-group button:active {
    transform: scale(0.96);
  }
  .btn-group button.primary {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .btn-group button.primary:hover {
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .tick-scale {
    position: relative;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .tick-scale::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 8px;
    right: 12px;
    width: 40px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    opacity: 0.4;
  }
  .tick-scale::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 8px;
    right: 12px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--line);
    opacity: 0.4;
    transform: translateX(40px);
  }
</style>
<div class="sgd-widget">
  <canvas id="stage" width="680" height="360" class="tick-scale"></canvas>
  <div class="controls-row">
    <label for="noise">噪声强度</label>
    <input type="range" id="noise" min="0" max="0.5" step="0.01" value="0.3">
    <span class="val mono" id="noiseVal">0.30</span>
    <span class="step-readout" id="stepReadout">步 5</span>
    <div class="btn-group">
      <button id="pause">暂停</button>
      <button id="reset" class="primary">重置</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function() {
    const root = document.documentElement;
    const tok = (n) => getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(n).trim();

    const canvas = document.getElementById('stage');
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    const W = 680, H = 360;

    let step = 5;
    let gdPos = [-2.5, 3.0];
    let sgdPos = [-2.5, 3.0];
    let gdPath = [[-2.5, 3.0]];
    let sgdPath = [[-2.5, 3.0]];
    let noiseScale = 0.3;
    let isRunning = true;

    function initPreWalk() {
      gdPos = [-2.5, 3.0];
      sgdPos = [-2.5, 3.0];
      gdPath = [[-2.5, 3.0]];
      sgdPath = [[-2.5, 3.0]];
      function grad(x, y) {
        const gx = x + 2.0 * Math.cos(2.5 * x) * Math.cos(1.8 * y) - 0.9 * Math.sin(3 * x);
        const gy = (y - 1) - 1.44 * Math.sin(2.5 * x) * Math.sin(1.8 * y);
        return [gx, gy];
      }
      const lr = 0.08;
      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        const [gx, gy] = grad(gdPos[0], gdPos[1]);
        gdPos = [gdPos[0] - lr * gx, gdPos[1] - lr * gy];
        gdPath.push([gdPos[0], gdPos[1]]);
        const [sgx, sgy] = grad(sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]);
        const nx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
        const ny = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
        sgdPos = [sgdPos[0] - lr * sgx + nx, sgdPos[1] - lr * sgy + ny];
        sgdPath.push([sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]]);
      }
      step = 5;
    }
    initPreWalk();

    const noiseInput = document.getElementById('noise');
    const noiseVal = document.getElementById('noiseVal');
    const stepReadout = document.getElementById('stepReadout');
    const pauseBtn = document.getElementById('pause');
    const resetBtn = document.getElementById('reset');

    function updateReadouts() {
      noiseVal.textContent = noiseScale.toFixed(2);
      stepReadout.textContent = '步 ' + step;
    }
    updateReadouts();

    function f(x, y) {
      return 0.5 * (x * x + (y - 1) * (y - 1)) + 0.8 * Math.sin(2.5 * x) * Math.cos(1.8 * y) + 0.3 * Math.cos(3 * x);
    }

    function toCanvas(wx, wy) {
      const cx = 40 + (wx + 3) / 6 * 600;
      const cy = 340 - (wy + 1) / 5 * 320;
      return [cx, cy];
    }

    function draw() {
      const ink = tok('--ink');
      const accent = tok('--accent');
      const line = tok('--line');
      const mute = tok('--text2');
      const bg = tok('--bg');
      const card = tok('--card');

      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);

      // 背景渐变
      const grad = ctx.createRadialGradient(340, 180, 20, 340, 180, 300);
      grad.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(180,120,200,0.15)');
      grad.addColorStop(0.5, 'rgba(100,160,220,0.12)');
      grad.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(60,60,80,0.05)');
      ctx.fillStyle = grad;
      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

      // 等高线
      ctx.strokeStyle = line;
      ctx.lineWidth = 0.5;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.25;
      for (let lev = -0.5; lev < 3.0; lev += 0.4) {
        ctx.beginPath();
        let started = false;
        for (let px = 0; px <= 600; px += 4) {
          const wx = -3 + (px / 600) * 6;
          for (let py = 0; py <= 320; py += 4) {
            const wy = -1 + (py / 320) * 5;
            const val = f(wx, wy);
            if (Math.abs(val - lev) < 0.08) {
              const [cx, cy] = toCanvas(wx, wy);
              if (!started) { ctx.moveTo(cx, cy); started = true; }
              else { ctx.lineTo(cx, cy); }
            }
          }
        }
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      // 极小标注
      ctx.fillStyle = mute;
      ctx.font = '10px ' + tok('--mono');
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.3;
      ctx.fillText('局部极小', 120, 280);
      ctx.fillText('全局极小', 480, 120);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      // GD路径 (从token取色)
      const gdColor = tok('--accent');
      ctx.strokeStyle = gdColor;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2.5;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.8;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i < gdPath.length; i++) {
        const [cx, cy] = toCanvas(gdPath[i][0], gdPath[i][1]);
        if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);
        else ctx.lineTo(cx, cy);
      }
      ctx.stroke();

      // SGD路径 (从token取色，用text2变体)
      const sgdColor = tok('--text2');
      ctx.strokeStyle = sgdColor;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2.5;
      ctx.setLineDash([6, 5]);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.8;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i < sgdPath.length; i++) {
        const [cx, cy] = toCanvas(sgdPath[i][0], sgdPath[i][1]);
        if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);
        else ctx.lineTo(cx, cy);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);

      // 当前点
      const [gx, gy] = toCanvas(gdPos[0], gdPos[1]);
      ctx.shadowColor = gdColor;
      ctx.shadowBlur = 12;
      ctx.fillStyle = gdColor;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(gx, gy, 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.shadowBlur = 0;

      const [sx, sy] = toCanvas(sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]);
      ctx.shadowColor = sgdColor;
      ctx.shadowBlur = 12;
      ctx.fillStyle = sgdColor;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(sx, sy, 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.shadowBlur = 0;

      // 图例
      ctx.font = '11px ' + tok('--sans');
      ctx.fillStyle = gdColor;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.9;
      ctx.fillText('全批量 (GD)', 540, 30);
      ctx.fillStyle = sgdColor;
      ctx.fillText('随机 (SGD)', 540, 48);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1.0;

      ctx.font = '12px ' + tok('--mono');
      ctx.fillStyle = mute;
      ctx.fillText('步 ' + step, 16, 22);
    }

    function stepOnce() {
      if (step >= 200) return;
      const lr = 0.08;
      function grad(x, y) {
        const gx = x + 2.0 * Math.cos(2.5 * x) * Math.cos(1.8 * y) - 0.9 * Math.sin(3 * x);
        const gy = (y - 1) - 1.44 * Math.sin(2.5 * x) * Math.sin(1.8 * y);
        return [gx, gy];
      }
      const [gx, gy] = grad(gdPos[0], gdPos[1]);
      gdPos = [gdPos[0] - lr * gx, gdPos[1] - lr * gy];
      gdPath.push([gdPos[0], gdPos[1]]);
      const [sgx, sgy] = grad(sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]);
      const nx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
      const ny = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
      sgdPos = [sgdPos[0] - lr * sgx + nx, sgdPos[1] - lr * sgy + ny];
      sgdPath.push([sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]]);
      step++;
    }

    let animId = null;
    function tick() {
      if (isRunning && step < 200) {
        stepOnce();
        updateReadouts();
        draw();
      }
      animId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    }
    animId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);

    noiseInput.addEventListener('input', function(e) {
      noiseScale = parseFloat(e.target.value);
      noiseVal.textContent = noiseScale.toFixed(2);
    });

    pauseBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      isRunning = !isRunning;
      pauseBtn.textContent = isRunning ? '暂停' : '继续';
    });

    resetBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      step = 0;
      gdPos = [-2.5, 3.0];
      sgdPos = [-2.5, 3.0];
      gdPath = [[-2.5, 3.0]];
      sgdPath = [[-2.5, 3.0]];
      const lr = 0.08;
      function grad(x, y) {
        const gx = x + 2.0 * Math.cos(2.5 * x) * Math.cos(1.8 * y) - 0.9 * Math.sin(3 * x);
        const gy = (y - 1) - 1.44 * Math.sin(2.5 * x) * Math.sin(1.8 * y);
        return [gx, gy];
      }
      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        const [gx, gy] = grad(gdPos[0], gdPos[1]);
        gdPos = [gdPos[0] - lr * gx, gdPos[1] - lr * gy];
        gdPath.push([gdPos[0], gdPos[1]]);
        const [sgx, sgy] = grad(sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]);
        const nx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
        const ny = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2 * noiseScale;
        sgdPos = [sgdPos[0] - lr * sgx + nx, sgdPos[1] - lr * sgy + ny];
        sgdPath.push([sgdPos[0], sgdPos[1]]);
      }
      step = 5;
      isRunning = true;
      pauseBtn.textContent = '暂停';
      updateReadouts();
      draw();
    });

    draw();

    const observer = new MutationObserver(() => { draw(); });
    observer.observe(root, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-theme'] });

    window.addEventListener('beforeunload', function() {
      if (animId) cancelAnimationFrame(animId);
      observer.disconnect();
    });
  })();
